  "id": "DrugBank_DB00494 - MONDO_10709",
  "verbalization": "Entacapone, a catechol-O-methyltransferase (COMT) inhibitor, is associated with the indication of Hereditary Late-Onset Parkinson Disease (HLOPD) through multiple pathways. These pathways link Entacapone to Pimavanserin and Istradefylline, both of which are indicated for Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome. The shared indication for HLOPD suggests a potential mechanistic overlap between these drugs and the syndrome. The evidence indicates that Entacapone may be repurposed for this condition, potentially through mechanisms involving COMT inhibition, which is a well-documented pathway in Parkinson’s disease. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Entacapone to the syndrome supports the hypothesis that it may exert a neuroprotective or neuroregulatory effect in early-onset Parkinsonism. However, the exact mechanism by which Entacapone influences the syndrome remains to be fully elucidated, and further studies are needed to confirm the therapeutic potential.",
